       {
        "lon": 34.3,
        "lat": 24.5,
        "text": "Eastern Desert",
        "size": 0.035,
        "color": "muted",
        "start": 1.0
       }
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "map_route",
     "narration": "And look at the borders. Egypt's western and southern borders are almost perfectly straight lines. They were drawn in agreements between colonial powers along lines of longitude and latitude, and they could be drawn with a ruler because almost nobody lived there.",
     "data": {
      "bbox": [
       20,
       17,
       40,
       33.5
      ],
      "highlight_countries": [
       {
        "name": "Egypt",
        "color": "accent",
