      "labels": [
       {
        "lon": 28,
        "lat": 23,
        "text": "SAHARA",
        "font": "display",
        "size": 0.08,
        "color": "muted"
       }
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "narration": "It isn't easy. In the desert heat, the river loses an enormous amount of water to evaporation along the way. Only a river fed by a huge rainy region thousands of kilometers away could survive this journey.",
     "data": {
      "kicker": "Desert heat",
      "text": "The river survives the Sahara because its water comes from far away",
      "highlight": [
       "far",
       "away"
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "narration": "And for thousands of years, the river did something even more important. Every summer, it flooded.",
     "data": {
      "text": "Every summer, the Nile flooded",
      "highlight": [
       "flooded"
      ]
     }
    }
