      }
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "list",
     "narration": "Their whole calendar followed the river. Three seasons: Akhet, the flood. Peret, the growing season. And Shemu, the harvest.",
     "data": {
      "title": "A calendar ruled by the river",
      "items": [
       "Akhet: the flood",
       "Peret: the growing season",
       "Shemu: the harvest"
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "narration": "They even built nilometers, stone staircases and wells that measured how high the flood rose. The higher the water, the bigger the harvest, and the more tax farmers paid that year.",
     "data": {
      "kicker": "Nilometers",
      "text": "Higher flood, bigger harvest, higher taxes",
      "highlight": [
       "taxes"
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "quote",
     "narration": "The Greek historian Herodotus summed it up about two and a half thousand years ago. Egypt, he wrote, is the gift of the river.",
     "data": {
      "text": "Egypt is the gift of the river.",
      "author": "Herodotus, 5th century BC",
      "highlight": [
